  "material": "Clearly recognizable weathered ferrous iron/steel plate with coherent dark exposed metal, flaking red-brown oxide, sparse pits and domed hammered rivet heads. It does not rely on resolution/sharpness or a material label for recognizability. Historical metallurgy is not established.",
  "formsAndScale": "Actual unchanged64px native and full1254px retained source viewed. BothdecodedMid256 andHigh512 preserve EIGHT heads:3top,2side,3bottom and no centrehead, with broad unsegmented plate between. Same-source Xregistration restores right margin. Native top/bottom middlehead x30/32 asymmetry is represented by common x31 compromise; this is a documented approximate fidelity choice, not exact landmark identity. Both32x32 and16x16 BOX native/replacement pairs remain representative in dark iron/rust balance, hardware count, scale, spacing and plate intention.",
  "repeatedEdges": "Viewed actual2x2tile repeats and actual1:1X,Y,XYcorner crops atboth tiers for RGB,height,XYZ and two opposed lights. Fine photographic plate seams at edges match the native intended square plate junction; no added relief perimeter bevel, duplicated half-rivet or new artificial horizontal stitch was demonstrated. The deliberate plate joint is visible and is not treated as a generic surface that should lose its native edgefeature.",
  "relief": "Viewed all8 complete decoded heads at1:1 in RGB,height,XYZ and neutral opposedlights atboth tiers. Source-measured head masks align to photographic silhouette; domes rise from shallow plate with rounded shoulders rather than separate litspot bumps or flat disc emboss. Opposed normals reverse illumination coherently. Eight4connected elevated heightcomponents at threshold.45 support count/placement, but visual shape classification remains primary. The colour plate seam remains fine colour/microstructure, without an authored high rim. Scalar head/plate difference is relative and does not establish runtime physical displacement depth.",
